is-server` as a fourth supervised child.  **Why this shape** - The product requires three distinct HTTP listeners and node-kill resilience; three OS processes (not one multi-bind process, not threads-only) match the grader???s SIGKILL model and the 60s auto-restart requirement. - FastAPI gives a single mountable `APIRouter` tree under `/api` so MARATHON-3+ can add modules without rewriting the HTTP entrypoint. - Redis is started now even though health does not use it, because later fan-out and the Redis-outage tests assume the daemon is owned by `start.sh`. - Language/framework are unspecified by the product instruction; Python 3.12 is present in the harness and fits REST + later WebSocket work.  **Alternatives considered** 1. **Node.js `http` / Express** ??? viable (Node is installed), but the rest of the epic???s backend tasks are naturally one shared Python package with SQLite; splitting runtimes would complicate shared state. 2. **Python stdlib only** ??? avoids deps, but forces every later task to reinvent routing, JSON validation, multipart, and WebSockets; rejected for velocity and consistency. 3. **One process binding all three ports** ??? fails the ???kill one HTTP node??? resilience model; rejected. 4. **Docker Compose / containers** ??? prohibited (no DinD / no remote orchestration).  **Trade-off accepted:** `start.sh` must ensure FastAPI/Uvicorn (and `redis` client later) are available via a local venv + pinned `requirements.txt`, preferably with wheels under `vendor/` so boot does not depend on live PyPI. Cold start is slightly heavier than stdlib, but the router seam for sibling tasks is far cleaner.  **Conventions this design locks for the epic (no sibling designs exist yet)** - Product name: **Huddle**; repo root is `/app` at runtime. - HTTP bind: `127.0.0.1` only; ports `8000/8001/8002`. - `node_id` ??? `{0,1,2}` derived solely from port (never from startup order). - API prefix: `/api/...`; JSON only for API responses. - Primary durable store (for later tasks): SQLite file at `/app/data/huddle.db` shared by all nodes via the local filesystem. Redis is **not** the source of truth for users/messages ??? it is for pub/sub fan-out (and optional caches) in later tasks. - Env contract for each node process:   - `HUDDLE_NODE_ID` ??? integer `0|1|2`   - `HUDDLE_PORT` ??? integer `8000|8001|8002`   - `HUDDLE_HOST` ??? `127.0.0.1`   - `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` ??? `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0`   - `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR` ??? `/app/data` (or `$APP_ROOT/data`) - Error bodies for unspecified errors: FastAPI default `{\"detail\": ...}` until a later design overrides. - Health **must not** check Redis or SQLite liveness; a live HTTP process alone is enough for `200`.  ## Interface Contracts  ### Process / ops seam (verifier ??? `start.sh`)  | Concern | Contract | |---|---| | Entrypoint | Verifier runs `/app/start.sh` (executable). | | Lifetime | `start.sh` stays in the **foreground** until killed; while it is alive the cluster serves. | | Children | Exactly three HTTP node processes + one `redis-server` (plus any short-lived helpers). | | Ports | HTTP: `127.0.0.1:8000`, `:8001`, `:8002`. Redis: `127.0.0.1:6379`. | | Restart | If an HTTP child exits for any reason (including SIGKILL  You are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line: REVIEW attempt=1 commit=e3282612631ec739f6e31b17e54d731898f7715f APPROVED ??? <reason> or REVIEW attempt=1 commit=e3282612631ec739f6e31b17e54d731898f7715f CHANGES-REQUESTED ??? <reason>\n10543 loom lead --backend cursor --prompt /installed-agent/loom-marathon/prompts-generic/critic.md --message REVIEW CONTRACT task=MARATHON-2 attempt=1 base=adb99cc7cca7c31e6f61695da0471dc55fc3b6c8 candidate=e3282612631ec739f6e31b17e54d731898f7715f  DESIGN: ## Summary  Deliver a bootable Huddle cluster skeleton at `/app`: a foreground `/app/start.sh` that launches