orts free'\npgrep -af 'huddle|redis-server 127' || echo 'no huddle procs'\nls -la start.sh .venv/bin/python 2>&1 | head\n# start fresh\nbash ./start.sh > /tmp/huddle2.log 2>&1 &\nSPID=$!\necho SPID=$SPID\nsleep 3\ntail -20 /tmp/huddle2.log\ncurl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health; echo curl_rc=$?\nps -p $SPID -o pid,cmd\npgrep -P $SPID -a || true","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"ports free\n10542 timeout 1200 loom lead --backend cursor --prompt /installed-agent/loom-marathon/prompts-generic/critic.md --message REVIEW CONTRACT task=MARATHON-2 attempt=1 base=adb99cc7cca7c31e6f61695da0471dc55fc3b6c8 candidate=e3282612631ec739f6e31b17e54d731898f7715f  DESIGN: ## Summary  Deliver a bootable Huddle cluster skeleton at `/app`: a foreground `/app/start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, plus `GET /api/health` returning `200 {\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":<0|1|2>}` with port???id mapping `8000???0`, `8001???1`, `8002???2`. This is the foundation every later API/realtime/SPA task mounts onto. No remote services and no Docker-in-Docker. Auth, workspaces, SPA, IRC, WebSocket fan-out, and durable schemas are out of scope here; this task only creates process supervision, shared config conventions, and a stub API router that subsequent tasks extend.  ## Technical Approach  **Decision:** One Python 3.12 process image, three OS processes, FastAPI + Uvicorn, supervised by bash `start.sh`, with local `redis-server` as a fourth supervised child.  **Why this shape** - The product requires three distinct HTTP listeners and node-kill resilience; three OS processes (not one multi-bind process, not threads-only) match the grader???s SIGKILL model and the 60s auto-restart requirement. - FastAPI gives a single mountable `APIRouter` tree under `/api` so MARATHON-3+ can add modules without rewriting the HTTP entrypoint. - Redis is started now even though health does not use it, because later 