a/huddle.db` shared by all nodes via the local filesystem. Redis is **not** the source of truth for users/messages ??? it is for pub/sub fan-out (and optional caches) in later tasks. - Env contract for each node process:   - `HUDDLE_NODE_ID` ??? integer `0|1|2`   - `HUDDLE_PORT` ??? integer `8000|8001|8002`   - `HUDDLE_HOST` ??? `127.0.0.1`   - `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` ??? `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0`   - `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR` ??? `/app/data` (or `$APP_ROOT/data`) - Error bodies for unspecified errors: FastAPI default `{\"detail\": ...}` until a later design overrides. - Health **must not** check Redis or SQLite liveness; a live HTTP process alone is enough for `200`.  ## Interface Contracts  ### Process / ops seam (verifier ??? `start.sh`)  | Concern | Contract | |---|---| | Entrypoint | Verifier runs `/app/start.sh` (executable). | | Lifetime | `start.sh` stays in the **foreground** until killed; while it is alive the cluster serves. | | Children | Exactly three HTTP node processes + one `redis-server` (plus any short-lived helpers). | | Ports | HTTP: `127.0.0.1:8000`, `:8001`, `:8002`. Redis: `127.0.0.1:6379`. | | Restart | If an HTTP child exits for any reason (including SIGKILL  You are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line: REVIEW attempt=1 commit=e3282612631ec739f6e31b17e54d731898f7715f APPROVED ??? <reason> or REVIEW attempt=1 commit=e3282612631ec739f6e31b17e54d731898f7715f CHANGES-REQUESTED ??? <reason>  Address this request using the lead mode conventions above.\n10579 /installed-agent/cursor-home/.local/bin/cursor-agent --use-system-ca /installed-agent/cursor-home/.local/share/cursor-agent/versions/2026.08.11-e8db854/index.js --output-format stream-json -p --force <!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic --> <!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).      Note: generic loom runs LOO